G5543.def:
χρηστός, -ή, -όν
(χράομαι), [in LXX chiefly for טוֹב (frequently of God: Psaumes 25:8, al.), also for יָקָר (Eze.27:22 28:13), יָשָׁר (Proverbes 2:21 א A) ;] 
serviceable, good; 
__(a) of things, good, pleasant: of food (as often in cl.), οἶνος, Luc 5:39; ζυγός, Matthieu 11:30 (EV, easy); in ethical sense, ἤθη, 1 Corinthiens 15:33; 
__(b) of persons, good, kind, gracious: Éphésiens 4:32; of God, Luc 6:35, 1 Pierre 2:3; τ. χρηστὸν (= ἡ χρηστότης) τοῦ θεοῦ, Romains 2:4.
†

G5587.def:
ψιθυρισμός, -οῦ, ὁ
(ψιθυρίζω, to whisper), [in LXX: Ecclésiaste 10:11 (לַחַשׁ) * ;] 
a whispering; 
__(a) of secret slander, 2 Corinthiens 12:20 (Plut.); 
__(b) of a murmured enchantment, Ec, l.with†

G5599.def:
ὦ 
interj., with vocat., 
O; 
__(a) in simple address (less frequently than in cl.; M, Pr., 71); Actes 1:1 18:14 27:21, Romains 2:1, 3 9:20, 1 Timothée 6:20; expressing reproof, Jacques 2:20; 
__(b) in exclamations of surprise, etc.: Matthieu 15:28, Luc 24:25, Actes 13:10, Romains 11:33, Galates 3:1; with nom. (Bl., § 33, 4), Matthieu 17:17, Marc 9:19, Luc 9:41.†
